From e4fb699815294ebbc98967ed0ebbe641acff3738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: geramyloveless <gloveless@jqluv.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:40:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom/AMDGPU] Release memory sources at issue only on gfx11

Consuming VMEM store VGPR sources and scalar memory sources at issue
(30246a9d6, c07086aa1) measured faster decode on gfx1151 for LSE's
qwen38-27b-q4 kernels (plain +2%, DFlash2 +6-22%) but 1-9% slower MTP
and DFlash2 decode on gfx1201. Add an issue-captured-sources builder flag,
set for the rdna3, gfx11_generic and rdna3_5 core descriptor sets. The
other sets keep the completion-released leases they had before those
changes: scalar address inputs until VMEM load, VMEM store or tensor
completion, and VMEM store VGPR sources until store completion, with the
amdgpu.store_source_reuse wait reason.

Test cases on the other sets take their previous expectations again,
low_memory_scalar_capture keeps its gfx11 cases, and the gfx1151
live_in_split_follows_entry_preamble case takes the combined register
reuse.
